"context": "Each figure read from a source had four lens columns: identity group, ICF code, access need and medical condition. Each held one code. (Since migration 131 they are held empty and a figure's codes are rows of the lens link table; this question is what led to it.) A determination has the same four columns and can already fill several at once, for example identity MOB together with the ICF code d450.\n\nYour answer to OR-1 says a determination should carry every relevant model. The crossing maps show that one identity group relates to several ICF codes: wheelchair users (MOB) map to d410, d420, d450, d455, d460, d465 and more, among them d450 Walking and d465 Moving around using equipment. A single figure about wheelchair users cannot name all of them in its one ICF column.\n\nD-0184 met the same shape in the old item layer and let one item have several link rows, one for each distinct combination of codes (A-18 by DEAF by AX-AUD beside A-18 by DEAF by AX-SPR), because they were different mechanisms and not duplicates. No source records a preference between the options below.",
